        "The tattooed man understands before you speak. People who have lived on a working plate learn the look of being spent. He sets down a cousin's bag. His hands do not shake now. The math has arrived at a number. \"Soft or quiet,\" Kane says, not unkind, which is the worst tone he has. You choose soft because you can still taste the house cup, or quiet because cover is a theology you have decided to join. The file will not record the difference as mercy. It will record it as method.\n\nSoft is money and a van and a story about a sister in a city with trees. Quiet is a cloth, a count, a body that will be found as a disturbance and not as a drawing of your face. Either way his eyes stop being a camera. That was the point. You will sleep. Radek told you what sleep costs. You are paying.",
