        "Voss finds you under a different leaking advertisement, same pill, same productive sleep. Her paper cup is empty. She has run out of coffee and substitutions. Up close she smells of van wound and the particular anger of a woman who still has a code.\n\n\"Tell me who you burned,\" she says. You tell her, or she already knows and is testing whether you will lie. She takes the sentence and puts it in the place where she keeps Ellis. \"All right. I am still here. That is not forgiveness. That is staffing. If you spent our leak I will make you carry the name for a year. If you spent Helix I will buy you a meal that isn't a vial. If you spent the witness I will not ask how. I will watch how you look at civilians and I will write it down.\"",
        "Rain finds the inside of her collar. She lets it. \"Kane appeared. Of course he did. He always appears when the file might walk. I cannot fire him. I can stand next to you while you decide whether his invoice is a life. Zero offered you owned. The street offered you cars. I am offering you a bed in a room that locks from the inside for four hours. After that the live test will come looking. I cannot cancel a client. I can make sure you sleep before they put a spotlight on your mouth.\"\n\nShe waits. Waiting is her version of the missionary thing, except she wants you out, not in. Out of what, you no longer know. Out is a map with water damage. A tram below throws gold onto her empty cup. She does not refill it. Empty is a statement she can still afford.",
