        "Marek's message arrives while Voss is still a wet shape. It is a clip, of course: you in the laundry court, mouth open on a breath, shirts falling, a caption in a typeface that wants to be intimate. Pell: this is the report. Crowe liked the still. Vale liked the pulse. I liked the way you got up. Live test will use this walk. Practice not looking like you have a soul if you plan to sabotage. If you plan to perform, practice the opposite. If you plan to run, I will enjoy the chase in a professional way.\n\nA second clip: Zero in the suite, watching a news crawl of Plate Nine, the fake park paused again. Zero does not text. They look at the camera as if they can see Marek's caption and find it tasteless. That look is a gift. You take it.",
