        "You say it to the flower and feel the suite's warm door in the words. Helix's for the hour. An hour can be enough if you let Vale set the terms. You send Crowe a still of your own face in the grate-light, which is the sort of offering she understands. She replies: good. wardrobe at nine. don't bring Voss's pistol unless you want it logged. You leave the pistol under the pillow for a future self who might be more Revelations than you are this morning.\n\nOwned or not, double or not, the sentence you spoke is a kind of PREP. It makes other people easier to agree with. It makes you easier too. You notice the ease and do not trust it. Not trusting ease is the last flinch. Kane paid for that flinch. Zero wants it gone. You walk down the stair with it ticking.",
