        "No one's. The flower believes you or it is paper. You send nothing. Silence is a door you have used before. It still works. It also makes both firms lean in. Heat is a kind of attention. You take the pistol and the biscuit crumbs and you leave the bolt unlocked, a small vandalism against Voss's poetry. She will notice. She will come uglier. You want that on the record of your body if not on a tablet.\n\nZero will be disappointed in a way they cannot dose. You hold that disappointment like a coal. Coals can start fires. Coals can also keep a hand warm. You have not decided which one you want. The unlocked bolt clicks behind you like a small insult you meant. Insults can be beacons. You walk toward collection anyway. Biscuit crumbs in your pocket feel like a civilian relic. You do not throw them away.",
