        "The theater is not called a theater on the doors. The doors say DEMONSTRATION SUITE B and a wellness mark that looks like a moth if you are unkind and a spine if you are on payroll. You walk a corridor lined with photographs of completed subjects who are all adults and all smiling with the same exactness Zero has. You do not look for Ellis. You look anyway. A face almost matches and then doesn't. Sequels.\n\nRadek is posted at the inner door, vest under a jacket, bruise-twin formal. He nods at your cloth. \"Unbroken,\" he says. \"Try to stay that way in a way I can respect.\" Marek is inside already, tablet hungry. Crowe will arrive when the client does, blackmail as hospitality. Vale is arranging a tray that is not Lyle's: instruments, scent, a vial, a contract.\n\nYou pause at the threshold and feel the rain deck still on your hair, the annex on your tongue, the curb in your feet. Whose car you chose is still a smell on you. Who you burned is still a color. The live test will not care, except as texture. You care. Caring is the distressed asset Kane mentioned. You spend it on one more breath that is yours.",
