        "Demonstration Suite B is warmer than a clinic and colder than a bedroom, which is the temperature of money. The chairs are the expensive kind from Zero's gallery. One of them will hold a client who buys export codes and daughters in the same sentence. The light is kind in the way Vale is kind. You stand on a mark that has been taped to the floor in a color that will not show on camera.\n\nOutside, the Stack reprints morning over last night's pulp. Inside, your name is about to be asked to do tricks. You can perform. You can sabotage. You can run. Zero did the first and lost a name. Ellis did something like the second and died on a form. Running is a story people tell in cities with trees. You have a pistol or you don't. You have PREP or you don't. You have a neighbor in a suite who paused a park.",
